4:
For me deadcode is unused and no longer needed code which should have been removed but it was not.
This dead, unutilised code still remains in the code base.

5:
Such unused code creates technical debt, because
- it consumes cognitive capacity, since you have to unserstand dead code sometimes.
- it has to be maintained, when a Python version is upgraded, you have to update all the code base including the unsued one.
- it might increase security risks,
    in case unsed code brought in outdated dependency with security vulnerabilities. 

Unused code consumes time, money and increases security risks.

It is like evil agents from the movie Matrix, who are waiting to cause you trouble.
We definitely want to get rid of it.

